From 3cb90a438506696e29e83ac85232190860d26322 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:42:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Carry per-picture metadata through ThreadedDecoder

ThreadedDecoder is now generic as ThreadedDecoder<M = ()>, with
decode_nal_with_meta and flush_with_meta returning (Frame, M) pairs, the
same as OrderedDecoder<M>'s on well-formed streams. The metadata stays
on the coordinator thread: it travels with the open picture, is stored by
sequence number with the GOP tag at dispatch, is paired with the frame at
commit, and rides in the reorder buffer as an Option. A field pair keeps
the metadata of its first field, as in OrderedDecoder. An unpaired field
that a later frame leaves behind has none: ThreadedDecoder<()> still
outputs it, as before, and the with_meta methods skip it.
ThreadedDecoder<()> keeps decode_nal and flush.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Sonnet 5.5)
